{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Factor Space Metric Shortcut.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Factor Space Metric Shortcut.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"factor space metric shortcut factor space metric shortcut","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Factor Space Metric Shortcut.md","fileName":"Factor Space Metric Shortcut.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Factor Space Metric Shortcut","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 10:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Scalable Hierarchical Search]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Scalable Hierarchical Search","datasciencefoundations_geometry.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Factor Space Metric Shortcut.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Factor Space Metric Shortcut.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"factor space metric shortcut factor space metric shortcut","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Factor Space Metric Shortcut.md","fileName":"Factor Space Metric Shortcut.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Factor Space Metric Shortcut","heading":"Factor Space Metric Shortcut","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The complete correspondence-analysis factor map preserves chi-squared distances among source profiles as Euclidean distances. When a task requires only a particular distance to an average profile, the book shows that it can be calculated directly from the original counts and marginals without computing every factor.\n\nFor massive data this can avoid a costly full eigenreduction while retaining the specified metric quantity. It does not provide the complete factor coordinates or every interpretation available from the full map; the shortcut is useful only when the requested measure is one of the identities preserved by that map.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Scalable Hierarchical Search","datasciencefou